  "verification_scope": "24 incoming-contact library cases (13 retained foundation plus11 SMS behavior cases), six selected library backup cases, provider integration8, schema integration4, recovery integration2, complete server library66 and canonical provider_flow3. Not all Store library/integration suites, full workspace, voice ambiguity or public administrative resolution qualification.",
  "behavior": [
    "Schema73 retains the recorded72 shape separately and extends custody reasons for uniquely routed, ineligible and historical-overlap observations. Its fresh-construction guard refuses to erase populated private custody. Normal opening of older pre-alpha schema still refuses with the existing backup/new-state boundary; no downgrade or compatibility path was added.",
    "Protected SmsObservation carries the original provider message resource separately from callback identity/digest, sender/recipient/body and provider time. Ordinary HTTP received messages require payload.id after raw signature/timestamp verification; signed controls retain their existing occurred_at ordering and no ordinary-resource requirement. Protected Rust callers and fixtures were updated to the desired API rather than a legacy wrapper.",
    "Overlapping SMS number pairs may now be explicitly configured. Current mounted verified Endpoint/account/route/member/delegate authority and bounded original audiences are considered together before any delivery. Multiple eligible candidates create one private hold with no Conversation message/journal event. Disabled, closed or unmounted retained policies belonging to the same configured account still prevent routing a late reply automatically to the remaining room.",
    "Unique eligible observations create custody and one real message atomically. Repeating the resource/content under another callback ID never delivers again, including after a real restore. Different content under an already-reserved resource is held as a resource conflict and cannot become another delivery. Originally ineligible resources are terminally ignored and cannot become assistant prompts after later enrollment.",
    "Administrative Store resolution selects only an original candidate, with current verified Endpoint/account/route facts, current delegate authority, original member epochs/roles, exact saved recipient ceiling and the same still-current enrollment grant. It writes an explicit original Participant audience, so a held all-message does not expand to new members. Account administration grants no Conversation history or message-body view.",
    "The selected real message, private audience/journal/fanout, one-resource delivery binding, shared logical-operation receipt and attributed audit commit in one transaction. Forced binding failure rolls back message, journal, decision and audit; replay commits once after recovery. Independent administrative database connections competing for different original candidates produce one decision and one message.",
    "Metadata exposes operator/credential/logical operation, selected candidate and local message/Session reference, with no held body/context/provider control URL and no history grant. Current authorization precedes completed resolution replay; Endpoint withdrawal refuses replay without rewriting the previously completed fact. Removed/readmitted membership cannot inherit an old candidate. STOP, account/delegate/Endpoint withdrawal and original consent restrictions refuse before delivery.",
    "All three canonical provider flows pass on current schema73 production code: signed SMS/Vapi private bounded context/reply/SMS delivery, HTTP/QUIC mutation replay, controls/signature/digest scope, early final callback while send remains pending, conflicting final callback refusal, cancellation/join/restart without resubmission. These do not yet exercise an administrative HTTP contact-resolution endpoint or voice hold/resolution.",
    "Current provider integration was updated to verified source/target Endpoint/account bindings and actual number-pair scope for an early final callback. Its later opposite terminal observation now explicitly expects the G6-044 conflict/reconciliation behavior while preserving delivered state. Failed old assumptions remain recorded; no SQL or callback invariant was weakened."
  ],
